From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:51:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: share a texture made unshared when its handle is asked
 for

Unity's video output (WindowsVideoTextureOutput) asks its own render
texture, which it made without D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED, for a shared
handle (IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle) once a frame, to open it with
OpenSharedResource, and gives up on the NULL that Windows returns there
("Got null handle from IDXGIResource::GetSharedHandle"): Valheim's intro
stayed black on Vulkan. Every device of a title is in one process on iOS, where
the memory of a shared texture is shared as a Metal heap within the
process (patches/wine-unix 0034).

On the first request for the handle of a texture made unshared, a
single-sampled 2D texture in GPU memory that the CPU does not map, the
image now moves to dedicated exportable memory, as a texture made shared
gets: DxvkContext::exportImage allocates the new storage, copies the
current contents there through relocateResources (the path that adds
usage to an image), and keeps the GENERAL layout a shared image has. The
copy is submitted at once, before another device can write the memory.
The image is shared from then on: it is not relocated again, and returns
to its default layout at each submission. The runtime description the
device that opens it reads has D3D11_RESOURCE_MISC_SHARED. The handle is
the memory's D3DKMT global handle; GetDesc still reports the texture's
own flags. A texture that cannot be shared this way, or a device that
cannot export memory, still gets NULL, and is not tried again.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-12-vulkan-unity-video-unshared-handle.md
Offered-upstream: no; in-process only (decision 0102)
---
